From 7191d2ad11ef14b6e7c62b1314e0801bfe6324f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew McCreath <andrew.mccreath@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 10:07:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: numeric field validation layer over the headcount fix

c16ef26 fixed the headcount renderer by taking the first numeric group.
That removed the visible bug but collapsed "422-458" to "422", inventing
precision the source never had, and left the same class of error live in
the other numeric fields.

- shared/numeric.ts: one rule, never strip non-digits and re-parse. Tokenises
  each number separately so a range can never be concatenated. Preserves
  ranges as "422 to 458" and flags them as estimates. Unit-aware parseMoney.
- shared/numeric.ts: crossCheckHeadcountAgainstRevenue. Absolute bounds cannot
  catch 422,458 because it is plausible in isolation; against $109M of revenue
  it is $258 per employee, which is not.
- shared/reportFieldRules.ts: registry of all 14 numeric fields reaching the
  UI, plus assertRulePathsExist, which fails a test when a rule targets a path
  the Zod schema does not define. That is how the original dead guard on
  financials.employees survived unnoticed.
- claude.ts: keeps FMP precedence from c16ef26, routes the rest through the
  shared normaliser, runs the registry, feeds a new confidence signal.
- claude.ts: unit-aware revenue growth; private-intel prompt no longer asks
  for a hyphenated range.
- utils.ts: formatHeadcount delegates to the shared parser so client and
  server cannot disagree about the same value.

